  "content": "Kojagrat Purnima: Farewell to Dashain, welcome to Goddess Laxmi\nOnlinekhabar\nMonday, October 6, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 6\nToday marks Kojagrat Purnima, celebrated as the farewell to Dashain and the welcoming of Goddess Laxmi.\nOn this occasion, devotees stay awake throughout the night, worshipping Goddess Mahalaxmi, the deity of wealth and prosperity. Kojagrat Purnima also signifies the conclusion of the 15-day Durga Paksha, popularly known as Bada Dashain, the greatest festival of Nepalis.\nAccording to religious belief, those who worship Mahalaxmi and remain awake tonight will receive her blessings of wealth and prosperity, as the goddess is believed to enter such homes during her earthly visit.\nThe festival holds special significance as it is observed 15 days prior to Laxmi Puja. Kojagrat Purnima is also known as Kaumudi.\nThe tradition of receiving Tika and Jamara, which began on Bijaya Dashami, officially concludes today on Kojagrat Purnima. The Nepal Panchang Nirnayak Samiti has stated that receiving Dashain’s Tika and Jamara until this evening, before the completion of all animal sacrifices, is considered scripturally valid.\nIn the morning, the remnants of flowers, offerings, and Jamara from Dashain rituals are taken to nearby rivers, ponds, or sacred water bodies for immersion.\nFrom tomorrow, the ritual of Kartik Snan (holy bathing in the month of Kartik) begins, along with the tradition of offering Akash Deep (lamps hung in the sky). This marks both the farewell to Dashain and the preparations for Tihar.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nCOVID-19 Nepal\nKP Sharma Oli\nNepal covid-19\nCPN-UML\nNepali Congress\nNepal\nNepalelection\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nDashain Tika continues on Ekadashi Day\n4 days ago\nMore than 5.5 lakh people exit Valley for Dashain\n6 days ago\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\n7 days ago\nDashain and the celebration of the sacred feminine amid social ironies\n2 weeks ago\nSheep and Himalayan goats brought to Sallaghari, Bhaktapur for Dashain\n2 weeks ago\nGhatasthapana performed at Hanumandhoka, marking the start of Dashain festival (Photos)\n2 weeks ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n15 hours ago\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n18 hours ago\nDisaster\nFloods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\n20 hours ago\nDisaster\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\n1 day ago\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n2 days ago",
